the russian invasion of ukraine is  entering a new phase  here's why eastern ukraine is key to  russia's military campaign and how  they're likely to attack  [Music]  the donbass area encompasses the region  of donetsk and luhansk essentially  running up the eastern side of ukraine  along a big chunk of the border with  russia  it has been at the heart of ukrainian  russian tensions for years  in 2014 russian-backed separatists took  control of large parts of the donbass  and have been at war with ukraine ever  since  the areas declared themselves separate  republics  just before the start of this latest  conflict russia formally and  unilaterally recognized the entirety of  the donbass region as being separate  from ukraine to  recognize the independence of donetsk  and lugansk people's republics  russian president vladimir putin then  declared contrary to fact that the  ukrainian government was undertaking a  genocide in the east  he started what he called a military  operation to stop this and achieve the  so-called de-nazification of ukraine  begin with the russians wanted to take  over the whole of ukraine they thought  they could do it within three days they  obviously couldn't then they thought  they could do it with a maneuver wall  whereby they took the cities  and moved in on kiev and surrounded it  they couldn't do that either  and so they're now in a third stage  which is where they're going for  something at least immediately far more  limited which is to consolidate their  hold in the southeast of the country in  the donbass and so territorially they're  now going for  about a sixth or a seventh of the amount  of territory they thought they would go  for to start with but this would be if  it succeeds  yet another bite into ukrainian  territory  the east of ukraine is home to large  communities of people who are ethnically  russian they speak russian  but for years many in the west have  accused putin of using this as an excuse  to increase russian influence over the  region  and it provided a reason to go to war  and take the land as his own  the fundamental mistake that putin and  his intelligence people and the military  made is assuming that just because  people in the donbass region were  russian speakers or even of russian  origin that they were not properly  ukrainian the fact is they're all  ukrainians and they deeply deeply resent  other than a pretty small minority being  invaded by a neighboring country  mariopol has been one of the worst  affected areas of the war  russian bombs and missiles have leveled  much of the city in an intense fight to  control it  geographically it's an important area  for russia to take with crimea in the  south under russian control since 2014  and the pro-russia separatists in the  donbass taking mariopol could create a  long stretch of land in the east  all under russian control  that's not the only reason why mariopol  is of strategic importance though it's  the major port in the sea of azov which  links into the black sea  and therefore handle a lot of material  so it's important because it's a port  and it's taken on a new strategic  significance because it's now the  southern anchor for this big  offensive the russians are beginning  and not least if mario paul somehow  somehow held out for very much longer  then it would it would be the david um  as it were refusing to be subdued by the  goliath of russian military power  [Music]  moscow has appointed a new general for  the ukraine operation  another signal that the war has entered  a new phase  general alexander dvornikov most  recently led russian forces in syria and  he was known for brutal tactics  targeting civilians  experts are calling the new focus of the  war the battle for donbass they will  undoubtedly be trying to create a more  maneuverous warfare in the southeast and  in one respect i think we'll see a lot  of tanks and armored vehicles trying to  move around quickly and ukrainians will  also be trying to move their heavy  equipment around their artillery but  also their anti-tank weapons to try to  slow down this this movement which the  russians are trying to create  it's thought that the russians want to  end this fight by the 9th of may russian  victory day marking the surrender of  nazi germany at the end of the second  world war it's an important date in  russia and it's marked by a large  military parade in  moscow this could mean that the conflict  is about to ramp up although how much  progress can actually be made in that  time bearing in mind the major losses  incurred by russia so far well that  remains to be seen  the ukraine resistance has been stronger  than most expected so far in this war  in the east forces are battle hardened  after years of fighting  but this new phase could push that to  the limit i think we will see bigger  movements of bigger units  moving around in this area once this  battle is uh really joined then i think  we'll see a really fierce battle at a  very high tempo  with a lot of attrition lots of losses  on both sides  cities in the region have encouraged  civilians to escape with humanitarian  corridors being set up but the death  toll is rising every day and this new  phase will only make that worse the  battle for donbass could be a key moment  in this war and one which neither side  can really afford to lose  you
 

